      "explanation": "The editorial promotes NRA Sighting-In Day and related hunting services. It is about hunting preparation and club activities, not firearm rules; excluded under the negative clarification."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "225",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "A 1930 send-off for the U.S. Free-Rifle International Team with fundraising appeals. Competition/marksmanship content only; no regulation discussed."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "226",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "The editorial analyzes FEC v. Wisconsin Right to Life and the BCRA 'electioneering communication' blackout — campaign-finance rules restricting broadcast speech — and judicial appointments. The rules at issue regulate election advertising, not firearms; gun-policy stakes appear only as consequences for NRA messaging. This does not meet the definition's requirement that firearm-regulating rules be the central subject. Ambiguity: the NRA framing invokes the Second Amendment, but mere mention does not suffice under the negative clarification."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "227",
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "The text systematically summarizes existing federal gun controls: the Federal Firearms Act of 1938 (licensing, interstate commerce restrictions, prohibited persons), the National Firearms Act of 1934 (taxes and registration of machine guns and other weapons), postal firearm-mailing restrictions, and the Federal Aviation Act weapon rule. Discussion of specific gun-control laws is expressly included."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "228",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "The editorial urges post-Christmas gun-safety instruction for boys. A passing reference to possible 'legislative restriction' as a reason for safety training does not make the central subject regulatory; it is safety education, which the negative clarification excludes."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "229",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "The text concerns General Westmoreland's endorsement of civilian marksmanship and the Army's withdrawal from the National Matches. It is about marksmanship training and defense policy; anti-gun editorialists' reactions are incidental, and no firearm rules are substantively discussed."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "230",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "A report on the 1936 NRA board meetings, Camp Perry improvements, National Matches, and team selection. Organizational and competition matters with no firearm regulation content."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "231",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "The editorial announces construction of a new NRA headquarters and describes the Association's mission and symbolism. It is organizational affairs; the recital of beliefs about lawful ownership and safety education does not substantively discuss firearm rules."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "232",
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "The central subject is 'cop killer bullet' legislation: the 1986 federal ban on armor-piercing ammunition, Rep. Schumer's proposed amendment to give the attorney general authority to ban bullets, and President Clinton's proposal that could ban common rifle cartridges. Ammunition bans and restrictions are core gun regulation under the definition and clarification."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "233",
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "Although framed as a response to internal NRA controversy, the editorial substantively discusses NRA's position on S. 914 (the McClure/Volkmer bill), its Senate testimony, acceptable amendments, and rebuttals of claims that NRA would support gun registration. The negative clarification excludes organizational affairs only 'when they do not substantively discuss firearm rules or policy proposals'; here a specific pending bill and registration policy are discussed in detail. Ambiguity: the piece is also about intra-organizational trust, which I weighed but found outweighed by the substantive legislative discussion."
    },
    {
      "document_id": "234",
      "label": "0",
      "explanation": "The text describes the Outdoor Education Project bringing shooting, hunting, and fishing instruction into schools. It is education/safety programming with no discussion of firearm laws; excluded under the negative clarification."
    },
    {
